      "short": "νₛ+δ(OCO) CO₂",
      "description": "Gas CO₂ combination of the infrared-forbidden symmetric stretch with the bend: the combined level is dipole-allowed although the stretch alone is not. Very strong and narrow, the most prominent gas band between 2200 and 1900 cm⁻¹, sitting squarely in the linear metal-carbonyl window, and the most misassigned band in this atlas: eight published studies read this one position as adsorbed CO. Its intensity tracks CO₂ pressure rather than anything on the surface, which is the discriminator. Heat and pressurise the cell and the same molecule adds hot and difference bands, absent at ambient conditions, at 2130 and 2094 cm⁻¹ among the carbonyls and 1079, 1050, 973 and 948 cm⁻¹ among the methoxy bands.",
