          "technique": "drifts",
          "wn": 2077,
          "note": "Table 3, band J: very strong and narrow, the Q branch of the 11101←00001 transition of ¹²C¹⁶O₂ and the most intense combination band in the range, which every other intensity in the paper is normalised to. Table 1 lists three earlier papers and Table 4 five more that assigned this position to adsorbed CO. Weaker gas bands are left undrawn: 2112 cm⁻¹, either this transition’s R branch or the P branch of a hot band, which the source cannot separate; 2130 and 2094 cm⁻¹, hot bands published as CO on Cu⁺ and on Cu(110); and 1933 and 1920 cm⁻¹, the 11102←00001 pair published as CO on a CuZn alloy. All of them need CO₂ pressure to show at all.",
          "tags": ["direct-dosing"]
        },
