          "note": "Fig. 5a and Section 3.3 (14% Co/Al₂O₃ at 220 °C, 30% CO + 60% H₂ + 10% Ar, ambient pressure): the P branch, on the high side of linear CO on cobalt. Subtracting a CO(g) spectrum taken over SiC at 50 °C fails at every scaling tried (Fig. 5b to 5e): too little leaves the branches positive, too much makes them negative and still leaves a spurious positive band near 2220 cm⁻¹, because the rotational envelope changes shape with temperature. A SiC reference at 220 °C in the same feed subtracts cleanly (Fig. 7b); the feed matters too, since H₂ conducts heat differently from CO and Ar."
