          "note": "Figs. S3a and S3b (DRIFTS, 5% CO/He flowing at 20 mL min⁻¹, 1 bar, 15 min): linear Cu⁰-CO at high coverage under dynamic conditions, at 30 °C on every catalyst and at 220 °C only on CuGa(0.15) and CuGa(0.20). That it survives to 220 °C on the Ga-rich samples alone is the paper's evidence that the promoter strengthens CO binding; on the unpromoted Cu and on loadings up to Ga/(Cu+Ga) = 0.10 no adsorbed CO is left at that temperature. Desorption at both temperatures is followed in Figs. S5 and S6.",
