          "measured_on": ["co_0", "co_al2o3"],
          "technique": "drifts",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Fig. 5a and Section 3.3 (14% Co/Al₂O₃ reduced in situ at 450 °C for 1 h in 60% H₂/Ar, then 220 °C, 30% CO + 60% H₂ + 10% Ar at ambient pressure, steady state, background SiC under Ar at the same temperature): a large band of linear, on-top CO on metallic cobalt, with ill-resolved bridged and multibonded CO below it. The CO(g) branches sit on its high side and only subtract cleanly against SiC at the same temperature and feed (Fig. 7b), which then leaves the same flat baseline as removing CO altogether (Fig. 7c)."
