          "note": "Fig. 4c and Section 3.2 (14% Co/Siralox reduced at 450 °C, then 80 °C, 30% CO + 60% H₂ + 10% Ar, background the same sample under Ar): the paper describes a cobalt carbonyl signal spanning 2100 to 1700 cm⁻¹ and gives only its maximum, without separating linear from bridged CO. It is recorded here because the maximum is where linear CO sits. The spectrum was taken to measure the gas path through the bed, for which the CO(g) R branch was used because it does not overlap this signal."
