          "measured_on": "cu_0",
          "note": "Fig. 7a, and Figs. S18/S19 in the SI (MCR-resolved, He+CO₂ vs H₂+He switching, 230 °C, 20 bar): CO* on metallic Cu at 2113 cm⁻¹ (Cu–Zn/SiO₂), 2115 cm⁻¹ (Cu/SiO₂) and 2108 cm⁻¹ (Cu–In/SiO₂), produced in situ by decomposition of κ²-HCOO*(Cu) rather than dosed — its rise mirrors the formate component's decay, making it the spectroscopic signature of the unselective RWGS branch. Invisible at steady state on every catalyst (it is hydrogenated away as fast as it forms); only the alternating CO₂/H₂ transient exposes it. Notably absent from Fig. S20 (Cu–Ga/SiO₂): no CO* is detectable on the Ga-promoted catalyst at all, which the authors take as the direct cause of its 94% methanol selectivity — formate spillover to Ga³⁺ outruns formate decomposition on Cu, so the RWGS branch never opens.",
