          "note": "Fig. 2A (3 % Au/SiO₂ pre-reduced in H₂, 1 % CO in He at 50 °C, 2 to 120 min; unpublished results reported in this review): a band at 2113 cm⁻¹ turns into one at 2076 through an isosbestic point, so one kind of site is converting quantitatively into another rather than two species growing side by side. The review's own conclusion for gold is three ranges: terraces near 2130 but unoccupied above 70 K, unreconstructed edges and corners 2115 to 2095, and the kinks and roughened edges of a CO-restructured surface 2080 to 2060 (p. 61). Silica cannot make oxygen vacancies, so the low band here is not negatively charged gold."
