          "note": "Sections 2.1 to 2.3 of a perspective; the numbers are from the RAIRS studies it reviews rather than from its own measurements. The singleton of atop CO on Pt(100), one molecule with no neighbours to couple to, is 2077 cm⁻¹, and coupling alone puts a line of five coupled CO 9 cm⁻¹ above it and a nine-molecule patch 16 above. Atop CO on Cu(110) moves only from 2088 to 2094 across the whole coverage range, a chemical redshift near −44 cm⁻¹ almost exactly cancelling a coupling blueshift near +50. The perspective's conclusion is that no observed band corresponds one-to-one to a kind of site: the bands are collective modes of the whole adlayer."
