        {
          "key": "Davydov.MolecularSpectroscopyOxide.2003",
          "state": "adsorbed",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Section 2.3.2, p. 96 of a monograph summarising infrared work on oxide surfaces rather than reporting one measurement, which is why no position, surface or sampling geometry is recorded here. Where the metal has d electrons to donate into CO's 2π*, a genuine carbonyl forms and ν(CO) falls below the gas-phase value: linear CO between 2100 and 1900 cm⁻¹, bridged below 1900, three-coordinated below 1800. The book's point is that one probe molecule reports two opposite things depending on the site, because a σ-only bond to a cation pushes the same band the other way instead."
