          "note": "Section 3 of a perspective, on the isotope-dilution method rather than on one spectrum, which is why no position and no sampling geometry are recorded here. The ¹³CO and ¹²CO singletons lie about 50 cm⁻¹ apart, enough to cut the coupling between a molecule and its neighbours by roughly an order of magnitude once one is diluted in the other; ¹³C¹⁸O against ¹²C¹⁶O gives 100 cm⁻¹ and cuts it further. Diluting at a fixed coverage separates the chemical and coupling halves of a coverage shift, and recovers bands that intensity transfer had hidden, such as CO on copper terraces. The perspective proposes running it under reaction conditions and names that MIOIRS."
