          "note": "Table 2, ν₂(OCO)ₐ: 1650 cm⁻¹ on α-Al₂O₃ (12.4 m² g⁻¹) and 1648 cm⁻¹ on γ-Al₂O₃ (101 m² g⁻¹), 274 mTorr CO₂ at 296 K. The two aluminas are recorded under one key because the paper's own finding is that they differ by a few wavenumbers at most, and it averages them for comparison with Fe₂O₃. On γ-Al₂O₃ the fully ¹⁸O-labelled species puts this mode at 1634 cm⁻¹."
