          "note": "CO₂ dosed on precipitated Ga₂O₃ at 300 °C (Fig. S12): of the three bands formed, this one is assigned to bicarbonate and the other two to carbonate. It is the least stable of them: Ar purging removes the bicarbonate while the carbonates stay, which is the paper's evidence that the carbonate, not the bicarbonate, is what the surface hydride goes on to reduce. Table S2 names the mode δ(OH) of CO₃H at 1634 cm⁻¹ rather than the OCO stretch this band records, the same label Rajput et al. use at 1650 cm⁻¹; the species is not in dispute, only which motion carries the band."
