          "note": "Operando DRIFTS, 230 °C, 10–20 bar, H₂/CO₂ = 3, Cu–M/SiO₂ from SOMC. MCR-ALS resolves two kinetically distinct κ²-HCOO* components. The Cu-bound one runs 2848 to 2860 cm⁻¹ across Figs. 4a/4c, 5b and 7a and the per-catalyst SI figures S15 to S20. It is the first and most abundant surface species on all four catalysts, and it exchanges to κ²-DCOO* within the 10 s acquisition limit under D₂, so formate formation and exchange are not rate-limiting; on Cu it is also the RWGS intermediate, its decay tracking the rise of CO* at 2108 to 2115 cm⁻¹. The promoter-bound component runs 2877 to 2896 cm⁻¹ and is clean only on Zn²⁺ (2896); on Ga³⁺ and In³⁺ it cannot be separated from Cu-bound formate and methoxy. Formate reaches the promoter by spillover from Cu, not by CO₂ activation on it: isolated M/SiO₂ without Cu converts no CO₂ at all.",
