          "note": "Fig. 5b/5c (MCR-resolved, Cu–Zn/SiO₂ SSITKA, CO₂+D₂ ⇄ CO₂+H₂, 230 °C, 10 bar): CD₃O* on silica at 2080 cm⁻¹, and at exactly the same position on the other three catalysts (SI Figs. S15/S16/S17) — unshifted by the promoter, consistent with methoxy sitting on the silica support rather than at the Cu–promoter interface. Unlike formate, this exchanges slowly, and its concentration profile — not the formate's — tracks the delayed appearance of gas-phase methanol, which is the observation that identifies methoxy hydrogenation/desorption as the rate-limiting step. Fig. S14c/d resolves the decay into a fast reactive pool (τ ≈ 1–6 min) and a slow spectator pool (τ ≈ 55–98 min); Fig. S12 is the linearised fit behind the KIE of 2.78. The asymmetric νₐₛ(C–D) partner is expected near 2160 cm⁻¹ and is not resolved, being buried under κ²-DCOO*.",
