          "key": "Phongprueksathat.KeyDriversActivity.2026",
          "state": "adsorbed",
          "measured_on": "sio2",
          "wn": [2985, 2994, 2996],
          "note": "Fig. 4a/4c (2985 cm⁻¹; the main text quotes 2981 cm⁻¹ for the same feature) and Fig. 5b (2994 cm⁻¹) — operando DRIFTS, 230 °C, 10–20 bar, H₂/CO₂ = 3, Cu–M/SiO₂ from SOMC. In the SI, Fig. S17 gives 2996 cm⁻¹ (Cu–In/SiO₂) and Fig. S20 2994 cm⁻¹ (Cu–Ga/SiO₂, labelled explicitly as adsorbed methanol inside a component non-separable from κ²-HCOO*(Ga³⁺) and CH₃O*(Ga³⁺)); Table S1 quotes 2996 cm⁻¹. Assigned there as νₐₛ(C–H) of molecularly adsorbed CH₃OH*, filed under this band on position rather than on that label, since gas-phase methanol's own ν₂/ν₉ assignment in this region is resonance-mixed (see νₐₛ(CH₂) MeOH below). Builds up only after ~90 min, and its delay relative to the mass-spectrometer CH₃OH signal is read as product methanol being re-adsorbed on silica rather than desorbing straight out.",
          "technique": "drifts",
          "tags": []
        }
      ],
      "intensity": "w",
