      "short": "Vₒ⁺ → CB ZnO₁₋ₓ",
      "description": "Not a vibration. An electron trapped in a singly ionized oxygen vacancy of reduced zinc oxide, lifted into the conduction band by the infrared beam itself. It absorbs as one featureless rise about 2000 cm⁻¹ wide running under the whole carbonyl and fingerprint region, so every band drawn on top of it sits on a sloping baseline rather than a flat one. Its maximum reports on the metal-oxide contact: near 1000 cm⁻¹ on zinc oxide alone and near 1500 cm⁻¹ once copper is present. It needs hydrogen to exist, vanishing under nitrogen, and is strongest under methanol synthesis conditions.",
