          "technique": "drifts",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Figs. 5 and 6, 30 bar. CZ, a coprecipitated Cu/ZnO with Cu:Zn 2.1:1, diluted to 8 wt% in KBr and activated in H₂ at 513 K; 3H₂/CO₂ at 20 NmL min⁻¹, 513 K, 4 cm⁻¹, 64 scans. Operando over 54 h with the outlet gas on a GC. Absent under N₂; it appears at once under pure H₂ with a maximum near 1400 cm⁻¹, and on switching to 3H₂/CO₂ it shifts to about 1500 cm⁻¹ (0.19 eV) and grows. It is strongest under methanol synthesis and falls back under intermittent N₂ or CO₂, but it does not follow the methanol production rate itself. Assigned to photoionization of Vₒ⁺ donor centres into the conduction band of the n-type oxide, and its intensity proposed as an online measure of the Cu-ZnO interaction. The main text puts the maximum near 1000 cm⁻¹ for copper-free ZnO, from a supporting-information figure not read here."
