          "state": "gas",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Fig. 2 right (in situ Raman, 1 wt % Cu/SiO₂ at 230 °C, 200 and 400 bar; Renishaw InVia, 532 nm Nd:YAG, 60 mW, 600 s accumulation through a micro-view-cell, SI p. S34). Marked on the figure with an open square as a band of the reactant mixture. The panel runs 1100 to 1800 cm⁻¹, far below the 4160 cm⁻¹ vibrational band, so what appears here is the pure rotational S branch of H₂. No position is printed for the marker, so this one was measured off the figure: the eight axis ticks are evenly spaced to within a pixel, which fixes the scale exactly, and the marker centre falls at 1248 cm⁻¹. The glyph shape could not be resolved at the printed resolution, so the line is identified by that position rather than by its symbol."
