      "short": "νₐₛ(DCD) CD₄",
      "description": "The triply degenerate stretch of methane-d₄, the deuterated twin of ν₃ in CH₄. Coriolis interaction splits the degenerate components into three sets of sublevels, so the band carries fifteen branches in all rather than five, and shows three Q branches instead of one. The number here is the band origin recovered from the rotational analysis; the three observed Q maxima straddle it.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
        {
          "key": "Shepherd.RamanSpectrumMethaned4.1957",
          "wn": 2258,
          "technique": "raman",
          "state": "gas",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Gaseous CD₄ at 1 atm, photographed on a grating spectrograph at 10.5 cm⁻¹ per mm with about 1 cm⁻¹ resolution, excited by the mercury arc (Hg 4047). Fitting the O⁰ and S⁰ branches gave a band origin of 2258.6 cm⁻¹, and the P⁰ and R⁰ branches fall on the same straight line, unlike CH₄ where they do not. Three Q branches are observed at 2250.9, 2257.5 and 2266.9 cm⁻¹ against 2250.0, 2256.8 and 2265.9 calculated. Coriolis splitting gives fifteen branches in all, the predominant intensity being in S⁺, Q⁰ and O⁻."
        }
      ],
      "intensity": "m",
      "width": "sharp",
